From ad699d03030616c711aae136c6fb256cdc1929b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Bodenham <matthew@bodenham.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:15:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 111/111] x1600: LCD fb descriptor tap (+0x1000 stderr log)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every write to LCD +0x1000 (the frame descriptor pointer stored by
lcdc_pan_display before the +0x1004 kick) logs the guest-physical value
to stderr ("x1600_lcd: fb descriptor @ %08x") — nothing else changes.
tools/fb-dump.py parses the tap lines from a QEMU stderr log, reads
desc+4 (strip the 0x80000000 flag bit), and extracts the 480x800 RGB565
frame from an HMP pmemsave guest RAM dump into a PNG (pure stdlib).
frame_num=2: the two descriptors (0x0250a000/0x0250b000 observed) each
hold their own frame line address, so the newest kick shows the visible
frame. Verified end-to-end: boot to the splash, pmemsave 0 0x4000000 at
the tap, PNG shows the stock HiBy R1 logo (the theme:1 logo1.jpeg
render, fb base 0x02600000).
---
 hw/mips/x1600.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/mips/x1600.c b/hw/mips/x1600.c
index f3b644a..1e8678c 100644
--- a/hw/mips/x1600.c
+++ b/hw/mips/x1600.c
@@ -1154,6 +1154,15 @@ static void x1600_lcd_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr,
         val &= ~1u;                     /* BUSY self-clears instantly */
     }
     s->regs[addr / 4] = val;
+    if (addr == 0x1000) {
+        /* fb readback hook (M3 prep): lcdc_pan_display stores the frame
+         * descriptor's guest-physical address here before the +0x1004
+         * kick; desc+4 holds the fb line address (yoff*stride + fb_phys,
+         * bit31 = flag). Logged to stderr for tools/fb-dump.py, which
+         * pulls the 480x800 RGB565 frame out of an HMP pmemsave dump
+         * (frame_num=2: either descriptor shows the visible frame). */
+        fprintf(stderr, "x1600_lcd: fb descriptor @ %08x\n", (uint32_t)val);
+    }
     if (addr == 0x1004 && (val & 1)) {
         /* frame kick: descriptor stored at +0x1000, EOF latches */
         s->regs[0x2010 / 4] |= 0x20000u;
